{#
  Single source of truth for closest-city weather data.

  Consumers: closest_city_sensor (configuration.yaml) and automations.
  Usage in any template:
      {% from 'cities.jinja' import closest_cities %}
      {% set cities = closest_cities() | from_json %}

  After editing this file, reload without restarting Home Assistant:
      Developer Tools > Actions > homeassistant.reload_custom_templates

  To add a city you need, in this order:
    1. A weather source for it (Settings > Devices > Add integration,
       e.g. Environment Canada or Met.no) - creates weather.* and
       sensor.<city>_* entities.
    2. For Met.no US cities only: derived sensors in configuration.yaml
       (clone the Atlanta block).
    3. One entry below.

  Fields per city:
    lat/lon     coordinates used for nearest-city detection
                (curated here on purpose - the coordinates stored by
                some integrations are unreliable)
    weather     weather.* entity id
    condition / temperature / high / low / summary
                available for every covered city
    humidex / uv_index / wind_chill / warnings
                Canadian (Environment Canada) cities only;
                omit keys that do not exist and consumers fall back
                to 'unknown'
#}
{% macro closest_cities() -%}
